\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Can every n-state one-way nondeterministic finite automaton be simulated by a deterministic two-way finite automaton with only polynomially many states, with the polynomial independent of the input alphabet?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Can every n-state one-way nondeterministic finite automaton be simulated by a deterministic two-way finite automaton with only polynomially many states, with the polynomial independent of the input alphabet?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
